      "text": "To determine the 2x2 matrix \\(\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\\) that satisfies the conditions given, we will work through these conditions step-by-step.\n\nFirst, consider the algebraic condition:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) into this equation:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nPer the matrix multiplication rules:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a \\cdot 3 + b \\cdot 0 \\\\ c \\cdot 3 + d \\cdot 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis results in:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe thus have the equations:\n\\[\n3a = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3c = 21\n\\]\n\nSolving these, we find:\n\\[\na = \\frac{6}{3} = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c = \\frac{21}{3} = 7\n\\]\n\nHence:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & b \\\\ 7 & d \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNow, consider the second condition:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute our already determined matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) into this equation:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & b \\\\ 7 & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nPer the matrix multiplication rules:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot (-1) + b \\cdot 5 \\\\ 7 \\cdot (-1) + d \\cdot 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis results in:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -2 + 5b \\\\ -7 + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe have the equations:\n\\[\n-2 + 5b = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -7 + 5d = -17\n\\]\n\nSolving these, we find:\n\\[\n5b = 3 + 2 = 5 \\implies b = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n5d = -17 + 7 = -10 \\implies d = -2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is in the boxed form:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
