      "text": "First, we denote the unknown matrix $\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}$. Then, multiplying both sides of the given equations by $\\mathbf{M}$, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}  = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\\\ bd \\\\ 0d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\\\ bd \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\\n&\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -a + 5b \\\\ -c + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -a + 5b \\\\ -c + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a & = 6 \\\\\n3c & = 21 \\\\\n-b + 5b & = 3 \\\\\n-d + 5d & = -17\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nSolving these equations, we see\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&3a = 6, \\\\\n3c = 21 \\therefore c = 7, \\\\\n-4b = 3 \\therefore b = -\\dfrac{3}{4}, \\\\\n-4d = -17 \\therefore d = \\dfrac{17}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer to the problem is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -\\dfrac{3}{3} & \\dfrac{17}{4} \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
